    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Kensington Manor is a private and exclusive enclave of just 13 homes arranged around a beautifully maintained, historic walled garden. Tucked away just off Rochestown Avenue, this peaceful development offers contemporary living in a tranquil, secure setting. No. 9 Kensington Manor is a beautifully presented 4 bed detached family home totalling c181sqm, combining elegant design with high-quality finishes in one of South Dublin's most desirable locations.\n\nThis light filled home offers generously proportioned and well-appointed accommodation throughout. On the ground floor, a stylish reception room flows seamlessly into a spacious family kitchen, complete with a large utility room and guest WC. To the rear, the family room has been thoughtfully extended by the current owners, providing a warm and welcoming space ideal for everyday living. Upstairs, the first-floor hosts two large double bedrooms, one ensuite along with a beautifully finished family bathroom. The top floor comprises two further double bedrooms both with ensuite shower rooms, including a luxurious principal suite with its own walk-in wardrobe and vault ceiling.\n\nOutside, the home is framed by mature hedging and shrubs, with a driveway offering off-street parking and an electric car charger. A gated side entrance leads to the landscaped rear garden, where a suntrap patio provides the perfect space for outdoor entertaining. A stylish garden room, ideal as a home office/gym offering further flexibility to suit modern family needs. One of the development's most unique features is the stunning formal walled garden, extending to approximately one acre. Originally planted during the Victorian era, the garden boasts mature box hedging, colourful borders, and a wide variety of flowering plants, trees, and shrubs creating a magical, private oasis and a dream area for children to play.\n\nFinished in full brick to the front and rear, the home reflects a lasting sense of quality and timeless design. With an A-rated BER, this property offers energy-efficient living without compromise. No. 9 Kensington Manor is a truly exceptional home in a rare and beautiful setting a perfect blend of modern convenience and historic charm.\n\nThis superb location needs little introduction, boasting close proximity to the vibrant hubs of Killiney, Park Point and Cornelscourt Shopping Centres, as well as the charming villages of Deansgrange, Blackrock, and Monkstown. The bustling town centre of Dún Laoghaire is also just a short distance away, offering a wide range of shops, restaurants, and amenities. Transport links are excellent, with the Quality Bus Corridor (QBC) only a few minutes' walk, ensuring swift access to Dublin city and beyond. The area is also renowned for its selection of top-tier primary and secondary schools, including Hollypark, Kill of the Grange, CBC Monkstown, St. Joseph of Cluny, Rathdown, Blackrock College, St Andrews and Loreto Foxrock, making it an ideal choice for families"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Special Features</li><li> Attractive detached red brick family home built in 2015</li><li> Four spacious double bedrooms and four bathrooms</li><li> Light-filled, well-proportioned accommodation extending to approx. 181 sq.m</li><li> Gas-fired central heating system</li><li> Solar panels</li><li> High-quality double-glazed windows throughout</li><li> Presented in superb decorative condition, oozes style and flair</li><li> Stylish designer kitchen with modern finishes</li><li> Family room with vaulted ceilings and southerly aspect</li><li> Guest WC, Utility and cloakroom</li><li> Contemporary bathrooms with high-spec fittings</li><li> Off-street parking to the front</li><li> Located in a private enclave of just 13 homes</li><li> Quiet cul-de-sac setting offering peace and privacy</li><li> Beautifully maintained period-style garden, ideal for children or a tranquil retreat with a BBQ area and a vegetable garden.</li><li> Residence management fee 1200, outside lighting and security cameras.</li><li> Excellent schools at both primary and secondary level, Holly Park national schools, Kill of the Grange NS, CBC Monkstown, Loretto Foxrock, St Joseph's of Cluny, Rathdown.</li><li> Excellent transport links with the QBC (Quality Bus Corridor) nearby (E2, L27, 7)</li><li> Surrounded by a wide range of local amenities</li><li> Within walking distance of Killiney Shopping Centre, Park Pointe Shopping Centre, and the villages of Monkstown and Deansgrange also close to Dún Laoghaire town centre</li></ul>"
      },
